cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "Pain and motor severity in early Parkinson disease: longitudinal analysis code"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a longitudinal study of pain and motor severity across six
  annual assessments of the Parkinson's Progression Markers Initiative, using a
  random-intercept cross-lagged panel model to separate stable between-person
  covariation from within-person change, inverse probability of censoring
  weighting for attrition, and a marginal structural model for time-varying
  confounding by dopaminergic dose.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nielspac177/ppmi-pain-motor-longitudinal"
keywords:
  - Parkinson disease
  - pain
  - PPMI
  - cross-lagged panel model
  - marginal structural model
  - reproducible research
